You are an insurance policy analyst. Read the policy and the claim, then return ONLY a JSON object, with no other text, using exactly this schema:
{"policy_number": string, "policy_type": one of ["commercial_property", "homeowners", "commercial_auto", "cyber_liability"], "insured": string, "effective_date": "YYYY-MM-DD", "expiration_date": "YYYY-MM-DD", "coverage_limit_usd": integer, "deductible_usd": integer, "exclusions": [{"peril": string, "has_exception": boolean}], "claim": {"peril": string, "decision": one of ["covered", "excluded", "covered_by_exception", "outside_policy_period"], "payable_usd": integer}}
Rules: list only exclusions that are still in force after any endorsements. Peril labels must come from this list: business_email_compromise, collision, data_breach, earthquake, fire, flood, flood_auto, freezing, hail, infrastructure_failure, intentional_damage, mold, phishing, power_failure, prior_known_breach, racing, ransomware, theft, unencrypted_device, unlicensed_driver, vandalism, war, wear_and_tear, windstorm. payable_usd = min(claim amount, coverage limit) minus the deductible, never below 0, and 0 when the claim is not covered.

